---
import Rechtstext from '../../layouts/Rechtstext.astro';
import Anbieter from '../../components/recht/Anbieter.astro';
import { anbieter, delivery, site } from '../../site';
import { routes } from '../../i18n';
---

<Rechtstext titel="Terms and conditions" pfad="/en/terms" beschreibung="Terms and conditions for buying a personal birth chart as a PDF from Horoskop-Geschenk.de.">
  <p class="nebentext">Last updated: {anbieter.stand.en}</p>

  <h2>1. Scope and provider</h2>
  <p>These terms apply to all orders placed via the website horoskop-geschenk.de. Your contractual partner is:</p>
  <Anbieter lang="en" />
  <p>Deviating terms of the customer do not apply.</p>

  <h2>2. What you buy</h2>
  <p>
    You buy a personal birth chart as a PDF file of {site.pages} pages, more than {site.pagesIndividual} of them
    individually calculated and written (one page more or less depending on the natal chart), in a light, a dark or
    both designs. It is calculated from first name, date, time and place of birth. The texts are created automatically on the basis of this calculation, following fixed rules of interpretation.
  </p>
  <p>
    Astrology is a system of interpretation, not a science. The horoscope does not predict events and is no
    substitute for medical, psychological, legal or financial advice. You are responsible for any decisions you make
    on the basis of the horoscope.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Ordering and conclusion of the contract</h2>
  <p>
    The presentation on the website is not yet a binding offer. You place one or more horoscopes in the cart, check
    all details there and can change or remove them at any time. By clicking “Order with obligation to pay” you
    submit a binding offer. The contract is concluded as soon as payment has been completed successfully.
  </p>
  <p>
    Immediately afterwards you receive an order confirmation by email. It contains the content of your order, these
    terms, the withdrawal policy and your consent to the start of creation. We do not otherwise store the contract
    text; please keep the email. The contract languages are German and English.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Prices and payment</h2>
  <p>
    One horoscope costs {site.priceLabel.en}, both designs together cost {site.bothPriceLabel.en}. All prices are
    final prices. <span class="platzhalter">{anbieter.steuer}</span> Payment is made in advance via our payment
    service provider Stripe, by card, PayPal, Apple Pay or the methods offered there.
  </p>
  <p>
    Voucher codes are checked and deducted at checkout. They cannot be redeemed for cash and can only be used once,
    unless stated otherwise on the voucher.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Delivery</h2>
  <p>
    The horoscope is sent as a PDF by email to the address you give when ordering, usually within
    {delivery.duration('en')} of receipt of payment. Please give an address at which you can be reached and also
    check your spam folder. If nothing arrives, get in touch and we will send it again.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Your details</h2>
  <p>
    The horoscope is based on the details you provide. You are responsible for their accuracy. Without the time of
    birth, the ascendant and houses cannot be determined; the horoscope is then less extensive, the price stays the
    same. If a typing error has crept in, let us know within 30 days of delivery and we will recreate the horoscope
    once free of charge.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Horoscopes as a gift</h2>
  <p>
    If you order a horoscope for another person, you enter their details. You confirm that you may use these details
    for the gift, for example because the person told you or because you know them as someone close to them. How we
    handle the data is described in the <a href={routes.datenschutz.en}>privacy policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Right of withdrawal</h2>
  <p>
    As a consumer you have a right of withdrawal in accordance with the{' '}
    <a href={routes.widerruf.en}>withdrawal policy</a>. It expires early if, when ordering, you expressly agree that
    we begin creation immediately and confirm that you thereby lose your right of withdrawal (section 356 (5) German
    Civil Code).
  </p>

  <h2>9. Use</h2>
  <p>
    The horoscope is intended for private use. You may print it, give it as a gift and pass it on to the person it was
    created for. Commercial use, resale and publication of texts or design are not permitted. The rights to the texts
    and design remain with us.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Defects</h2>
  <p>
    The statutory rights for defects of digital products apply (sections 327 et seq. German Civil Code). If a file is
    faulty, incomplete or unreadable, let us know and we will supply a correct version. Not liking an astrological
    interpretation is not a defect.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Liability</h2>
  <p>
    We are liable without limitation for intent and gross negligence, for injury to life, body or health and under the
    Product Liability Act. In the case of slight negligence we are only liable for the breach of an essential
    contractual obligation, meaning an obligation whose fulfilment makes the contract possible in the first place and
    on which you may rely. In this case liability is limited to the foreseeable damage typical for the contract.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Dispute resolution</h2>
  <p>
    We are neither obliged nor willing to take part in dispute resolution proceedings before a consumer arbitration
    board. If you have questions or problems, simply write to us and we will find a solution.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Final provisions</h2>
  <p>
    German law applies, excluding the UN Convention on Contracts for the International Sale of Goods. If you are a
    consumer, the mandatory consumer protection provisions of the country in which you have your habitual residence
    remain unaffected.
  </p>
  <p class="nebentext klein">This English version is provided for convenience. In case of doubt, the German version applies.</p>
</Rechtstext>
